# Privacy-check toggle (process-options.md "Commit identity & anonymity";
# .githooks/{pre-commit,commit-msg,pre-push}, scripts/check_privacy.py). One
# value on the last line:
#   true                     — RUN the privacy gate: the commit author email and
#                              committed content (staged diff, message, repo
#                              sweep, outgoing range) are scanned for PII /
#                              identity leak classes; a private (non-exempt)
#                              email or a machine-local path blocks. The
#                              exempt-email allowlist lives in
#                              scripts/check_privacy.py (EXEMPT_EMAILS).
#   false (default) / absent — OFF: the privacy gate is skipped. The always-on
#                              secrets floor (docs/secrets-scan) still runs.
#
# This gate defends PRIVACY (keep a real, contactable person out of commits),
# NOT identity/attribution — which account authored is the user's own git
# config, not a value pinned here. The gate only enforces that whatever identity
# is used, and whatever lands in content, is not private. (Supersedes the old
# docs/commit-identity email-pattern policy.)
false
